    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0463" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg249"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 68.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Mr. Blair</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 21, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> This Department has received a note from
                    the minister for foreign affairs of Costa Rica, requesting a detail of two
                    scientific engineers for the purpose of surveying a route for a wagon-road or
                    railway between San José and the Atlantic.</p>
                <p>In the note a promise is made that the salaries and expenses of the engineers
                    shall be promptly paid. Inclosed is the reply of the Department under a flying
                    seal which you may close after reading the answer, which you will then deliver
                    to Mr. Montufar.</p>
                <p>You will notice that although his request has been acceded to, the names of the
                    engineers have not yet been determined upon and nothing is said about their
                    compensation and expenses.</p>
                <p>Before they set out, however, it may be prudent that some definite provision, for
                    the latter at least, should be made in advance by that government.</p>
                <pb facs="0464" n="250" xml:id="pg250"/>
                <p>You will consequently lose no time in endeavoring to mate a satisfactory
                    arrangement upon this point, of the result of which you will apprise the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
